--- the plan, which changes nothing
CONVERT-ACCOUNT: 1 file(s) to sqlite
  CAOLD
  2 directory file(s) left alone -- name FROM dir to include them
listonly: nothing was changed
--- so CAOLD is still where it was
CAOLD                    lmdb
--- FROM names one backend and leaves the rest alone
CONVERT-ACCOUNT: 1 file(s) to lmdb
  VOC (last)
listonly: nothing was changed
--- FROM and the target agreeing is nothing to do
CONVERT-ACCOUNT: FROM and the new type are both lmdb -- nothing to do
--- VOC moves, and it moves last
CONVERT-ACCOUNT: 1 file(s) to lmdb
  VOC (last)
  2 directory file(s) left alone -- name FROM dir to include them
converted 1 file(s) to lmdb
--- a FRESH process finds the moved VOC, and every record is still there
VOC                      lmdb
5 record(s) counted
--- the whole account, VOC last again
CONVERT-ACCOUNT: 2 file(s) to sqlite
  CAOLD
  VOC (last)
  2 directory file(s) left alone -- name FROM dir to include them
converted 2 file(s) to sqlite
CAOLD                    sqlite
5 record(s) counted
--- the directory file was left alone throughout
CABP                     dir
--- a wrong target converts nothing and says so once
  FAILED CAOLD: cannot create the new nosuchdrv file (bad type or connection?)
CONVERT-ACCOUNT: stopping -- the first file failed, so the
  target is wrong rather than the file.  Nothing was converted.
CAOLD                    sqlite
--- FROM dir includes the source directories and still refuses CATALOG
CONVERT-ACCOUNT: 2 file(s) to sqlite
  BP
  CABP
  CATALOG is never converted -- it holds executables
converted 2 file(s) to sqlite
CATALOG                  dir
caseed ran
